  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: A homely meal that has withstood the test of time,
    cherished for its simplicity and warmth. The royal family used to serve this
    to their people to herald the coming of the new year, and the shelterless Verehnians
    would hold their bowls tight just to restore some feeling into their fingers
    in the cold dark night. It is an uncommon sight now. These days, people can only
    afford to dream of hot soup warming their hands.
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: There is a story of a man living on the streets
    of Verehn, wandering around, clutching a bowl of soup, hoping against hope that
    the heat from it would combat the night chills. But a bowl of month-old soup
    can only do so much. Strangely, the next morning, when his friends pulled the
    bowl from his cold, unyielding death grip, the soup was mysteriously warm. Care
    to taste the warmth of a human soul?
